{"component_id_namespace":"ec077a53-0b40-5f21-b1fe-a62094d2476b","component_schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","components":[{"attributes":{"code":"TMC","legacy_node_id":"ks-topeka:tmc:2.40.120","page_type":"section"},"citation":"2.40.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","content_hash":"9a51906d46b01411199d75f74e9762088adcbff20bc957add8b690c637b9b54a","heading":"Law enforcement officers – Employment – Powers.","ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":null,"schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:section","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","text":"The City Manager may employ law enforcement officers who shall have power to execute all process issued by any Municipal Judge within the State and delivered to him or her for that purpose, to detain persons, to place them in custody, and to arrest them, pursuant to the terms of this article.\nThe powers of law enforcement officers with respect to the code of criminal procedure shall not be reduced by this Code. (Ord. 20206 § 9, 9-10-19; Ord. 18477 § 9, 7-12-05; Ord. 17666 § 11, 3-27-01. Code 1995 § 50-46. Formerly 2.110.120.)\nCross References: Police Department, TMC 2.20.090 .\nState Law References: Similar State statute, K.S.A. 12-4111 .","type":"section","workbench_component_id":"92f92efa-d600-59ce-8135-072ad29d713a"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","content_hash":"c5b200e09eb37971f0a3a7e7b9938916253655193977c2993f102a2b291fdacc","heading":null,"ordinal":0,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:block:0","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","text":"The City Manager may employ law enforcement officers who shall have power to execute all process issued by any Municipal Judge within the State and delivered to him or her for that purpose, to detain persons, to place them in custody, and to arrest them, pursuant to the terms of this article.","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"29f43ec0-f6ea-57b1-a66d-86ff19385920"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","content_hash":"5af00d3ff39295e5850a533554b7d33f0530151fc9f660c1771fbd90516da0a9","heading":null,"ordinal":1,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:block:1","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","text":"The powers of law enforcement officers with respect to the code of criminal procedure shall not be reduced by this Code. (Ord. 20206 § 9, 9-10-19; Ord. 18477 § 9, 7-12-05; Ord. 17666 § 11, 3-27-01. Code 1995 § 50-46. Formerly 2.110.120.)","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"40014a57-b42b-5dc4-8d66-1b28e503f7ab"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","content_hash":"b3690706389bc36b62ec0c62b3dea31a6dd0c29e5778164c15b68f9d4f0aa5e3","heading":null,"ordinal":2,"parent_source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:section","schema":"exais.workbench_component.v1","source_component_key":"ks:city:topeka:municipal-code:tmc:2.40.120:block:2","source_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","text":"Cross References: Police Department, TMC 2.20.090 .","type":"paragraph","workbench_component_id":"1fde1f29-b7ab-5824-ad22-2c174c268e71"},{"attributes":{"block_kind":"paragraph"},"citation":"2.40.120","citation_url":"https://topeka.municipal.codes/TMC/2.40.120","content_hash":"b1d6eb0514bbd784ac7b6c506c1fd48761f07fc52ee600cabe87b5f83aae813b","heading":null,"ordinal":3,"parent_source_compone